Subject: [PATCH] dvfel: transport complete 12-bit FEL pictures in a TV-led carrier

Keep composed chroma as RG32F until top-left 420-to-422 reconstruction and
12-bit quantization. Negotiate a TV-led RGB888 carrier with bit 4/status 4,
independent of the incompatible old tunnel and diagnostic linear12 formats.
Serialize source VDR DM and supported extension blocks into framed HDMI
control-data packets with CRC, parity and three repetitions. Resolve compressed
DM against the preceding full fixed fields; never send the raw HEVC RPU NAL.
For single-track combo input, associate sibling NAL 62 mapping and DM with
BL presentation PTS for both SW and HW EL decoding. Reorder EL pixels by
display order independently; missing BL metadata cannot borrow an EL AU RPU.
Preserve source scene flags in parsed DM. Until the kernel reports an actual
TV-led display start, force refresh only in upload copies. Assign output IDs
from effective display metadata and recalculate every packet CRC; retain exact
fixed diagnostic packets and the parser cache.

Preserve the original legacy 10-bit quantization path. The linear12 diagnostic
format remains available but S5 MIF probes show its low two bits are truncated.
TV-led jobs without valid metadata report passthrough for the kernel to drop.
Bypass DI when either packed output mode is selected at playback startup.
Explicit debug modes separate the picture and DM: 2 uses R10 grey bars plus
its exact DM71 packet, 3 keeps video with DM71, and 4 keeps real DM with grey
bars. Temporary uploads never change the real RPU cache.
Optional startup-only serial pass profiling reports its explicit glFinish
wall-time overhead; an explicit 4/6-tap marker retains 6 as the default.
For strictly matching 10-bit identity mapping and power-of-two NLQ, replace
prediction/residual LUT reads with equivalent highp arithmetic. Retain the
half-code deadzone, EL interpolation and all 12-bit/metadata output bytes;
other mappings use the existing LUT path.
An optional startup marker enables an exact OpenCL neutral-EL backend. Inspect
every complete decoded EL image before selecting the fast route, retain source
DM per frame, and fall back to GLES for non-neutral EL or unsupported metadata.
Compile before registering jobs and import the actual dma-bufs without copies.
An opt-in driver-owned RGB24 output pool removes the publication copy; validate
the full token and current job, write only its assigned slot and finish before
DONE5. Drain before fallback/teardown and stop on uncertain GPU ownership.

An opt-in output session prepares native BYPASS while the GPU starts, then
uses the existing Kodi display transaction. Its owner protocol separates
first-picture dequeue from visible output and transmitter readiness. Keep
the original refresh preference and restore the saved processing controls
after the GUI transaction. The companion 9912 patch supplies the codec,
renderer and Amlogic window lifecycle hooks; the marker is off by default.

This replaces kodi-9910-dvfel-linear12-output.patch; do not apply both.
